    <item>
      <title>Ordeal of the Demon King</title>
      <author>- Tarnagh -</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/712592</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/712592#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">0fec021c7b495b2c6503c4478fe61dcbdfddf78e</guid>
      <pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:16:25 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad8e02dee7d8.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad8dd4486bca.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad8dd44959b4.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad8dd449830e.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad8dd44c12aa.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; v3.3.0&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Adjustment&lt;/em&gt;: Phantom Ganon's position changed&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Tweak&lt;/em&gt;: Ganondorf's behavior tweaked&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Optimization&lt;/em&gt;: No wildlife spawns when duelling&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Created by &lt;strong&gt;Tarnagh&lt;/strong&gt;. Bow model and texture by &lt;strong&gt;The Hidden Yiga Clan&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Ordeal of the Demon King&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"You have faced monsters, Dragons, and gods. But have you ever stood before the Demon King himself?"&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Ganondorf stands, and he is waiting for you. Not for a battle. He has watched the bearer of the Master Sword from afar, counted his victories, and now he intends to find out for himself whether the hero is worth anything at all.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
This is a full quest line: dialogue, choices that stick, a duel of his choosing, three commissions that end with weapons no one else in Hyrule can give you - and, for those who survive him, paths no one else can open.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Demon King&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
He offers you a choice.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Kneel.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;strong&gt;Or refuse.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Choose carefully. The Demon King does not offer his mercy twice.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Ordeal&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Those who bow before him earn something granted to almost no one: the chance to prove themselves in single combat, against an opponent he picks personally.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Survive, and he will admit - grudgingly, in his own way - that you are more than another hero clinging to a dying world. Refuse the duel, and the ordeal ends where it began, beneath his gaze.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
The moment you accept, the sky turns the red of a Blood Moon, an unseen wall closes around the ground he has chosen, and his Phantom rises to face you - its name and its strength written across the top of your screen. Nothing else living is allowed inside: this is a duel, not a hunt. Try to run, and the ground itself will bring you back.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
He does not sit this one out. He watches from inside the circle, in the stance he takes before he strikes - and he will be watching until one of you falls.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The King's Will&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
A proven hero is a useful hero, and the Demon King has work.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
His first commission sends you after the horns of three Silver Lynels, thirty of Naydra's spikes, and a horn taken from the Light Dragon herself. Bring them, and he will forge you a bow out of them, by hand, in front of you.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"Watch closely as their fragile light is consumed by my darkness."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
And the world answers him. While he forges, gloom boils up around him and the sky and earth turn the red of a Blood Moon - and when the rite is done, the colour drains away again.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
The bow he hands over is not an ordinary one. Frost clings to it and never melts, it throws a faint light of its own, and it will outlast anything in your pack. &lt;strong&gt;And its arrows freeze.&lt;/strong&gt; Not once, not while a material is fused to them - always.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;em&gt;Read that twice before you install:&lt;/em&gt; there is exactly one arrow actor in the game, so &lt;strong&gt;every arrow you loose, from any bow, leaves winter behind it&lt;/strong&gt;. That is the price of the Demon King's gift, and it is paid by your whole quiver.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
But do not mistake his favour for friendship. You serve his purpose for exactly as long as you remain useful.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Horn of the Demon King&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"Take this. A horn of my true form. A manifestation of the doom that awaits this fragile world."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Come back to him carrying his bow and he will ask more of you - if you are willing to hear it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
This time he wants the horns of all three elemental Dragons, and two from the Light Dragon. What he makes of them is not a weapon but a piece of one: &lt;strong&gt;a shard of the form he has not yet taken&lt;/strong&gt;, fused from their elemental essence and his own dark magic.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Fuse it to anything you like:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;+90 attack&lt;/strong&gt; - well past anything the base game offers&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fire in every form&lt;/strong&gt; - it sets what it strikes alight, explodes in flame, keeps you warm, and does not go out&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shatters armour&lt;/strong&gt;, fells trees, and throws further&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;Shield's features: &lt;strong&gt;guard bonus, perfect-parry bonus, shield bash and counter&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
It cannot be sold. Some things are not for rupees.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Thunderstorm Spear&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"There was a spear, warrior. I wielded it before this world learned to fear me."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Bring him the horn and he will ask once more - and this time it is not a trophy he wants rebuilt, but a weapon he carried before Hyrule had a name for him. Thirty shards from Farosh's spikes, four saber horns from the silver lynels, and the horn of the Light Dragon again.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"Stand back. Let the heavens bear witness."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
What he returns to you is the &lt;strong&gt;Thunderstorm Spear&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;45 attack&lt;/strong&gt;, and a reach half again past any spear in the game&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;It comes back.&lt;/strong&gt; Throw it and it returns to your hand - and it does not shatter on whatever it hits on the way&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lightning in every form&lt;/strong&gt; - it electrifies what it strikes, bursts in a shock, and never runs dry&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guard bonus and perfect-parry bonus&lt;/strong&gt;, an expanded shockwave, a faster charge, and warmth in the cold&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Breaks a guard at 80&lt;/strong&gt; - more than two times what it was&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;Iron, and no one told the sky. Carry it into a storm and see what comes looking for it&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No hand holds it.&lt;/strong&gt; It rides at Link's side, a little above and apart, point turned ahead - and it swings, throws and returns without ever being gripped&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
It is a spear, so it is fast; it is his, so it is far too strong for one. And it was never made to be carried: the Demon King's storm does not ask to be held.&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Forged Anew&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Weapons break, and he knows it. Come back without the bow, without the horn, or without the spear, and he will say what he thinks of you - and then take the materials again.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"Did the storm prove too much for your grip? It answered to me long before it ever answered to you."&lt;/em&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;The Demon King's Path&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;"Name a place, then the ground between here and it will cease to matter."&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
Once his trial is behind you and his first commission given, your conversations with him can end with a request: &lt;strong&gt;open a way for me&lt;/strong&gt;. He answers with the same dark rite he forges with - and then the world folds, and you are somewhere else.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
Seven places, some of them closed to you any other way:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Old Throne Room&lt;/strong&gt; - the Sanctum in Hyrule Castle&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Floating Coliseum&lt;/strong&gt; - five Lynels, and the Depths all around&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Thunderhead Isles&lt;/strong&gt; - the storm that hides the relics of the Zonai&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Imprisoning Chamber&lt;/strong&gt; - the very tomb of the prologue, where he was sealed&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beneath Hyrule Castle&lt;/strong&gt; - Gloom's Approach, the heart of his malice&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beneath the World&lt;/strong&gt; - below the Depths themselves, where there is nothing at all&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Western Plateau&lt;/strong&gt; - ground beyond the walls Hyrule raised to keep its world small&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
A few words of warning, because he will not give you any:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;In the &lt;strong&gt;Imprisoning Chamber&lt;/strong&gt;, do not walk on towards the Demon King's own cutscene. Leave the way you would leave anywhere else - by the map.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beneath the World&lt;/strong&gt; means exactly that. You may arrive on gloom - do not let it take away your life. &lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Features&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Demon King:&lt;/strong&gt; Ganondorf as he ought to be - imposing, calculating, merciless, and worthy of his title. His words are written in red.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Choices that stick:&lt;/strong&gt; what you say to him is remembered across saves, and he remembers it too.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The King's Trial:&lt;/strong&gt; a duel against an opponent he chooses for you - under a Blood Moon sky, inside a circle you cannot leave, with a boss's life gauge, and with the Demon King watching in his own battle stance.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;His Wrath:&lt;/strong&gt; strike him, shoot him or bomb him outside the duel, and he answers with a line of his own - and your death.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nothing is a dead end:&lt;/strong&gt; every commission can be taken again if what he made is gone, and the hand-in is the same rite - not a copy of it.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Three commissions:&lt;/strong&gt; hunt across Hyrule for materials no shop sells, and watch him forge them by hand - gloom, sound and a blood-red sky included. Lose what he made and he will forge it again.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Three unique rewards:&lt;/strong&gt; a bow whose arrows always freeze, the Horn of the Demon King, and the Thunderstorm Spear - which no hand holds.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Demon King's Road:&lt;/strong&gt; seven destinations across the surface, the sky, the Depths, and places the game never meant you to reach.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;No new NPC clutter:&lt;/strong&gt; one existing character carries the whole thing. The only other change to the world around him: two wolves step aside, and nothing else alive enters the circle while you fight.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Technical Specifications&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;For developers and modders:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Host actor:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;Npc_BaseCampSoldier_Hylia005&lt;/em&gt; - renamed, re-scripted, and given Ganondorf's pack. No new actor is registered.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quest logic:&lt;/strong&gt; EventFlow, in his own flowchart - branches, talk choices, pouch queries and autosaves.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Map logic:&lt;/strong&gt; two Logic modules (AINB) of the mod's own, cloned node by node from vanilla ones. One returns a player who leaves the duel through a vanilla warp event. The other watches an area at his feet on the &lt;em&gt;PlayerAttack&lt;/em&gt; layer (and one for bombs) and opens his own conversation through his vanilla &lt;em&gt;EventSetting&lt;/em&gt; row.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The duel ring:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;AirWallForBossBattleField&lt;/em&gt; - the only wall that holds when placed by a mod - with its visible effect switched off. Wildlife is kept out by a vanilla &lt;em&gt;ForbidAutoPlacementAreaOnlySphere&lt;/em&gt;, present only during the duel.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;His battle stance:&lt;/strong&gt; a private animation graph - a copy of the Hylian male graph with the boss's &lt;em&gt;Default_Lockon_Wait&lt;/em&gt; cloned in - selected by a &lt;em&gt;ConditionalSchedule&lt;/em&gt; on the duel flag.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Persistence:&lt;/strong&gt; ten booleans appended to &lt;em&gt;GameDataList&lt;/em&gt;, with &lt;em&gt;MetaData&lt;/em&gt; resized to match so they actually reach &lt;em&gt;progress.sav&lt;/em&gt;. They are appended, never inserted, so an existing save keeps every field where it was. Two more live only within a session and are never saved.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dialogue:&lt;/strong&gt; Mals, built from genuine vanilla 1.2.0 archives. His lines carry the inline red colour code; your choices stay white.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Teleportation:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;GameSystemActor.EventReserveBancChange&lt;/em&gt; by named start position. Two are vanilla (&lt;em&gt;OpeningStart&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;StartPos_HyruleCastleIncident&lt;/em&gt;); five are added to the &lt;em&gt;MainField&lt;/em&gt; and &lt;em&gt;MinusField&lt;/em&gt; start-position tables. The menu is three steps of four choices - the most a single talk event can show.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Custom equipment:&lt;/strong&gt; Crystallized Ice Bow (&lt;em&gt;Weapon_Bow_166_For_Ganondorf&lt;/em&gt;), Horn of the Demon King (&lt;em&gt;Item_Enemy_39&lt;/em&gt;), Thunderstorm Spear (&lt;em&gt;Weapon_Spear_166&lt;/em&gt;, the Gloom Spear). All three are vanilla actors with rows in every registry - no new actor is registered anywhere.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Freezing arrows:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;NormalArrow&lt;/em&gt; gets the three fields that distinguish a Gleeok's ice beam from its ordinary one - &lt;em&gt;ChemicalType Ice&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;DamageElements [Ice]&lt;/em&gt;, &lt;em&gt;InitialIceMagic&lt;/em&gt; - each in a file of the mod's own name, with a private parameter table. Tulin's arrow, which inherits from it, is pinned to the vanilla table. &lt;strong&gt;It is the only arrow actor in the game, so this affects every bow.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compatibility:&lt;/strong&gt; no file that other packs share by path is edited. A mod manager that rebuilds packs from shared files (TKMM) would otherwise carry such an edit into every other pack with that path - which is exactly how an earlier version froze King Gleeok's beams alongside &lt;em&gt;Depths of the Kingdom&lt;/em&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The returning spear:&lt;/strong&gt; a boomerang in TotK is four things, not one - the &lt;em&gt;Boomerang&lt;/em&gt; subtype, &lt;em&gt;IsBreakByThrownAttack: false&lt;/em&gt;, an &lt;em&gt;Atk_Thrown&lt;/em&gt; collider, and the &lt;em&gt;Boommerang_Catch&lt;/em&gt; attention client (Nintendo's own spelling). All four are copied from &lt;em&gt;Weapon_Lsword_174&lt;/em&gt;; miss the last and the weapon will not even equip.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The spear that is not held:&lt;/strong&gt; its mesh is moved inside the model itself - sideways, up, and turned point-forward - because TotK gives a weapon offsets for crouching, riding, sheathing and standing, but none at all for the plain state of being in a hand. The sheathed pose has its own knob, &lt;em&gt;SheathTransOffset&lt;/em&gt;, so back and hand are set apart. The hit shapes stay in Phive where they were, so the spear strikes from the hand it never occupies.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Durability:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;em&gt;MaxLife&lt;/em&gt; lives in two places - the registry row and the pack's own &lt;em&gt;LifeParameters&lt;/em&gt; - and the pack wins. Both are written, or nothing changes.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
  &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resource table:&lt;/strong&gt; every entry the mod grows is recomputed and shipped.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;The Ordeal Awaits&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;em&gt;Stand before the Demon King. Prove your worth. And remember - he is the one deciding whether you deserve to live.&lt;/em&gt;</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/ordeal_of_the_demon_king_164e5.zip" type="application/zip"/>
