      <title>BotW Abilities</title>
      <author>HanSoloBlaster</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/726588</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/726588#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">716cc0c7f3106ee810efb02c98d620c03c5b12f1</guid>
      <pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 04:58:09 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aee7d105151b.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6aee7cc42c071.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad846f1df1e9.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad846f213948.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ad846f25f3bb.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6acb8ef6c86e8.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6adcdd3ac5bdf.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6acb8ef791359.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6acb8ef791a94.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6acb8ef732d57.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6acb8ef60bdae.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6acb8ef7d4e83.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; Support for TotK 1.4.3&lt;br&gt;&lt;p&gt;Emulator only (for now).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;BotW Abilities&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;br&gt;Adds &lt;b&gt;Stasis+, Cryonis and Remote Bombs&lt;/b&gt; from BotW to TotK. Also adds the champion abilities from BotW: &lt;b&gt;Urbosa's Fury, Revali's Gale, Mipha's Grace and Daruk's Protection&lt;/b&gt;. Also now adds &lt;b&gt;Wolf Link&lt;/b&gt;, a companion you could play with via an amiibo in BotW. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Note that these are &lt;b&gt;merely shoddy approximations of the original abilities&lt;/b&gt;. They &lt;b&gt;don't&lt;/b&gt; have the exact appearance and behavior of the originals. Also please respect that this is essentially an &lt;b&gt;alpha version&lt;/b&gt; of the mod. There will be bugs and the user experience isn't currently great. I intend to fix these things. &lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;How to use&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stasis&lt;/b&gt;: hold L1, then tap R1 and select Stasis from the second ability page to enter preview mode. Press A over an object to freeze it for ten seconds (enemies for five). Afterward, subsequent hits to objects will build momentum as it works in BotW. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Remote Bomb&lt;/b&gt;: The sphere and cube bomb now show at the front of your materials quick view and materials in the main menu. Hold, throw or fuse them to arrows. Tap L to detonate. Alternatively, select the from the second ability wheel by holding L1, then tapping R1 and selecting the bomb icon of choice. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cryonis&lt;/b&gt;: hold L1, then tap R1 and select cryonis from the second ability page to activate preview mode. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;Most abilities act like native TotK abilities - the most recent ability is accessed with a tap of "L".&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Champions&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Revali's Gale&lt;/b&gt;:  Press jump once and hold the jump button. You'll see an effect charge underneath Link. Once it is fully charged, release jump. May use three times before recharge is needed. Recharge before collecting Tulin's Sage's Vow is 6 minutes, after it is 2 minutes.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Urbosa's Fury&lt;/b&gt;: Perform a charged weapon attack; the attack must be charged not just once but twice. All enemies in the surrounding 50m radius will be struck with lightning. May use three times before recharge is needed. Recharge before collecting Riju's sage's vow is 12 minutes, after it is 4 minutes.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Daruk's Protection&lt;/b&gt;: Hold the shield and you'll be surrounded with an orange-tinted orb (really just Sidon's water shield) that protects you from a strike once per use. May use six times before recharge is needed. Recharge before collecting Yunobo's sage's vow is 18 minutes, after it is 6 minutes.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Mipha's Grace&lt;/b&gt;: Prevents death and restores hearts to max. May use only one time before recharge is required. Recharge before Sidon's sage's vow is 24 minutes, after it is 8 minutes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Wolf Link&lt;/b&gt;: A companion who will follow you, try to fight enemies and just be a good boy in general. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;Recharge times reflect the recharge times from before and after finishing the Champion's Ballad DLC from the original game. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;All champion abilities can be enabled/disabled via a custom medallion in the inventory. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Requires Tears of the Kingdom 1.2.1.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Emulator&lt;/b&gt;: extract the archive and copy its `BotW Abilities` folder into the game's mod folder, then enable it in the add-on list. &lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Switch&lt;/b&gt;: copy the 0100F2C0115B6000 folder into atmosphere/contents/.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Known Issues&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;b&gt;Stasis:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Target/selection often requires you to be somewhat close.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Stasis' "arrow" showing magnitude and direction of momentum is fairly inaccurate to the BotW version. It mostly updates in a straight line based on Link's forward position and doesn't update based on angle of weapon attack like in BotW&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Wolf Link&lt;/b&gt; is kinda stupid. He doesn't know how to path-find properly and frequently gets stuck. He is also easily distracted, or doesn't follow you well enough. He should try to summon nearby you when he gets lost, but sometimes he doesn't. It's better to treat him as a fun nearby pet than as a serious fighting companion.  &lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt; &lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Development&lt;/h2&gt;Developed and tested on the Citron emulator, Ryubing and Switch hardware. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;All (freely MIT licensed) source code and a more detailed README.md can be found &lt;a href="https://github.com/afiaka87/totk-mods/tree/main/botw-abilities" target="_blank"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;AI Disclaimer&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This project was developed with heavy help from AI Claude Opus 5.5 and Sol 6.1. For an overview of how I develop ExeFS mods using AI please see this post &lt;a href="https://gamebanana.com/posts/13964739"&gt;https://gamebanana.com/posts/13964739&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Donations&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you enjoy my work, feel free to &lt;a href="https://buymeacoffee.com/hansoloblaster" target="_blank"&gt;buy me a coffee&lt;/a&gt;! I provide the mod and its source code completely free and open source. I stand by that; so only donate if you're feeling friendly or would like to boost my spirits!</description>
      <media:content url="https://files.gamebanana.com/mods/botw-abilities-v023-switch-subsdk7.zip" type="application/zip"/>
