    <item>
      <title>Material Columns</title>
      <author>HanSoloBlaster</author>
      <link>https://gamebanana.com/mods/733845</link>
      <comments>https://gamebanana.com/mods/733845#PostsListModule</comments>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">0279e438b6b95195558979c5393e9ac7370591d7</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:38:32 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae3ef6bc9d4e.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae3ef6bccaec.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae3ef6bea1ee.jpg"/&gt;&lt;img src="https://images.gamebanana.com/img/ss/mods/6ae3ef6becfdf.jpg"/&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Update:&lt;/strong&gt; Fieldworks, Support 1.2.0, 1.4.2&lt;br&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Material Columns&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;h3&gt;v0.1.6&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Added to &lt;a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://gamebanana.com/mods/739060"&gt;Zonai Fieldworks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Added support for TotK 1.4.3. Tested on Switch.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;The same download still works on 1.2.0, 1.2.1 and 1.4.2.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;v0.1.4&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Column labels are translated to your game's language.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;p&gt;Materials from other mods can be put into categories with an INI file.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Material Columns&lt;/h1&gt;&#13;
Group the materials quick-select menu into columns by category, as a 5th sorting option, alongside the original four.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;b&gt;Quick links:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.com/afiaka87/totk-mods/tree/main/material-columns" target="_blank"&gt;README/Source&lt;/a&gt; &lt;span class="GreyColor"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.com/afiaka87/totk-mods/blob/main/material-columns/docs/CATEGORY-CONFIG.md" target="_blank"&gt;Custom Material Docs&lt;/a&gt; &lt;span class="GreyColor"&gt;|&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href="https://buymeacoffee.com/hansoloblaster" target="_blank"&gt;Buy me a coffee&lt;/a&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Description&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
This mod changes the materials quick-select menu so that materials are grouped into columns of various categories. You can still use the original four sorting options.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;How to Use&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Open:&lt;/b&gt; hold &lt;b&gt;D-pad Up&lt;/b&gt;, then press &lt;b&gt;Y&lt;/b&gt; until &lt;span class="OrangeColor"&gt;Material Columns&lt;/span&gt; appears.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pick a column:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;Right Stick&lt;/b&gt; left/right.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Pick a material:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;Right Stick&lt;/b&gt; up/down.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;How to Install&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Emulator&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&lt;ol&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Extract to the game's mod directory.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Enable &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;material-columns&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;/ol&gt;&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Switch&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&lt;ol&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Extract the download.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Drag the extracted &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;0100F2C0115B6000&lt;/span&gt; folder into &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;atmosphere/contents&lt;/span&gt; on your SD card.&lt;/li&gt;&#13;
&lt;li&gt;Merge the folders. &lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;You need both exefs and romfs.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&lt;h2&gt;Custom Material Actors for Other Mods&lt;/h2&gt;&#13;
As of v0.1.4, other mod authors and users can pin custom materials to existing or new columns. To do this, add an INI file to your mod's RomFS folder at &lt;code&gt;romfs/MaterialColumns/Categories/your-mods-name.ini&lt;/code&gt;. The file should follow the format described &lt;a href="https://github.com/afiaka87/totk-mods/blob/main/material-columns/docs/CATEGORY-CONFIG.md" target="_blank"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;span class="OrangeColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Note:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;i&gt;This is a first version and the design of this system may change.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Add a Material to an Existing Column&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="BlueColor"&gt;[General]&lt;/span&gt;&#13;
Version = &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;span class="BlueColor"&gt;[Materials]&lt;/span&gt;&#13;
Obj_RemoteBombSphere = &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;special-materials&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;
This places the botw-abilities actor for the spherical remote bomb in the existing &lt;code&gt;special-materials&lt;/code&gt;&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Create New Columns&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="BlueColor"&gt;[General]&lt;/span&gt;&#13;
Version = &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;span class="BlueColor"&gt;[Category.example.sky-fruit]&lt;/span&gt;&#13;
Name.en-US = &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Sky fruit&lt;/span&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;span class="BlueColor"&gt;[Category.example.crystals]&lt;/span&gt;&#13;
Name.en-US = &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;Crystals&lt;/span&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;span class="BlueColor"&gt;[Materials]&lt;/span&gt;&#13;
Item_Example_Cloudberry = &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;example.sky-fruit&lt;/span&gt;&#13;
Item_Example_Sunplum = &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;example.sky-fruit&lt;/span&gt;&#13;
Item_Example_StormCrystal = &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;example.crystals&lt;/span&gt;&#13;
Item_Example_Mooncap = &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;mushrooms&lt;/span&gt;&#13;
Item_Example_WildPear = &lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;fruit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&#13;
This creates two new columns, &lt;code&gt;example.sky-fruit&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;example.crystals&lt;/code&gt;, and assigns fictional actors to them and to the existing &lt;code&gt;mushrooms&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;fruit&lt;/code&gt; columns.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Translations and Further Reading&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
You can provide translations as shown in &lt;a href="https://github.com/afiaka87/totk-mods/blob/main/material-columns/docs/examples/fictional-materials.ini" target="_blank"&gt;this lengthier example&lt;/a&gt;. For a comprehensive overview of everything that can be done, including examples for a few existing mods and the names of the built-in columns, see &lt;a href="https://github.com/afiaka87/totk-mods/blob/main/material-columns/docs/CATEGORY-CONFIG.md" target="_blank"&gt;the docs&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
&lt;h3&gt;Compatibility&lt;/h3&gt;&#13;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class="GreenColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Supported:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt; TotK &lt;b&gt;1.2.0, 1.2.1&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;1.4.2&lt;/b&gt; only, for now. Tested on a Switch.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class="RedColor"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Not compatible:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt; my Fleet Sync mod or any other subsdk6 mod.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&#13;
&#13;
&lt;hr&gt;&#13;
